# DapperDemo — project overview

A learning project for Dapper: a cross-platform **Avalonia** app for a
pet-sitting business ("Patas & Passeios"). Identifiers, comments and docs are
English; the UI text is Brazilian Portuguese.

`README.md` (repo root) holds the intended entity model and a screen-by-screen
spec. Read it before adding a feature — but treat it as a *design* document: it
has drifted from the code in places (see **Known drift** below).

Everything below assumes you are in `DapperDemo/` (the solution directory, one
level under the repo root). `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root is the fuller companion
narrative for this same guidance; keep the two in step when you change either.

## Commands

```bash
dotnet build app/DapperDemo.Desktop/DapperDemo.Desktop.csproj   # Linux/Windows head + full desktop chain
dotnet test  tests/Tests.Dapper/Tests.Dapper.csproj             # the only test project
dotnet run   --project app/DapperDemo.Desktop/DapperDemo.Desktop.csproj
```

- Prefer building the **Desktop head** over `dotnet build DapperDemo.sln` on
  Linux/CI: the iOS/Android/MacOS heads need mobile workloads that a plain SDK
  image does not have, so the full-solution build fails on them.
- **Building while a head is running fails** with `MSB3027`/`MSB3021`: the
  running process locks `bin/`. That is a lock, not a code error — stop the app
  or build only the project you changed.
- Toolchain: **.NET 10** (`net10.0`), Avalonia **12.1.1**. First checkout must
  init the submodule (`git submodule update --init --recursive`) or restore
  fails with `NU1105`.

## Layer graph

```
Repository.Dapper (src/1. Contrato) ← DTOs, repositories, SQLite/Dapper, backup
  ↑
DapperDemo.Viewmodel               ← presentation models, commands, session
  ↑
DapperDemo.View                    ← .axaml + code-behind, theme, components
  ↑
DapperDemo.Infrastructure          ← composition root
  ↑
Desktop / MacOS / iOS / Android    ← platform heads over the same View
```

- Assembly/root namespaces are `DapperDemo.<Project>`; the data layer is
  `DapperDemo.Repository.Dapper` (project file `Repository.Dapper.csproj`).
- `src/` contains only `1. Contrato`. The numbered sibling folders from the
  original template are gone — do not recreate them. Portuguese folder and
  test-project names are legacy; leave them, write English inside them.
- The MVP/navigation/DI/control infrastructure lives in the **AvaloniaFramework**
  submodule at `external/AvaloniaFramework`, consumed by `ProjectReference` (not
  NuGet). Editing framework source takes effect on the next `dotnet build`; this
  repo pins a framework commit, so after changing it, commit/push there and
  `git add external/AvaloniaFramework` here. The **data layer deliberately does
  not reference the framework** — it uses `ConfigureAwait` rather than the
  framework's `WithSync()`/`NoSync()` helpers, the one place that is correct.

## Build-system deviations (these bite if assumed away)

- **Central package management is off.** `Directory.Packages.props` declares no
  `PackageVersion` items — **package versions live in each `.csproj`**. Adding a
  package means adding the version where the reference is.
- **No `stylecop.json` at the solution root.** It ships inside
  `AvaloniaFramework.Development/build/` in the submodule and is attached as
  `AdditionalFiles`. Do not add a local copy.
- **StyleCop is enforced at build time** via `Directory.Build.targets` importing
  the submodule's analyzer targets (`EnforceCodeStyleInBuild`), tuned by
  `Default.Analyzers.ruleset`. If the submodule is missing, the build warns
  loudly and analysis silently stops.

## Dependency injection

The container is AvaloniaFramework's own, **not** `Microsoft.Extensions.DI`.
Each layer owns a `ContainerBuilder` under `DependencyInversion/`.

- Adding a view or view model means registering it in **both**
  `DapperDemoViewContainerBuilder` and `DapperDemoViewmodelContainerBuilder`
  (with `.WithAbstractions()`). A miss fails at **runtime**, not compile time.
- Data-layer singletons (`DapperDatabaseService`, the repositories,
  `BackupArchive`) are registered in `DapperDemoInfrastructureContainerBuilder`.
- Anything needing a `TopLevel` cannot live in a view model: put an interface in
  `DapperDemo.Viewmodel/Services/` and an Avalonia impl in
  `DapperDemo.View/Services/`, registered `CreateSingleton<Impl>().WithAbstractions()`
  in the View builder (e.g. `ImagePicker`, `UriLauncher`, `BackupFileDialog`).
  Interfaces are **not** `I`-prefixed, matching the framework's convention.

## Testing

`tests/Tests.Dapper` covers the **data layer only** (repositories, migrations,
money rules) — run it before touching any of them. The view models have no
tests, so anything in `DapperDemo.Viewmodel` is verified only by running the app.

## Known gaps & drift (real, not aspirational)

- **Android head does not start**: Avalonia 12 replaced
  `ISingleViewApplicationLifetime` with `IActivityApplicationLifetime`;
  `App.axaml.cs` and the submodule's `AvaloniaNavigationController` only handle
  the former. Deploy with `dotnet build … -t:Install`, never a bare `adb install`.
- **Hotel income is understated**: `RepositoryServices.GetMonthlyIncomeAsync`
  sums the daily rate, not rate × nights, so the Perfil headline disagrees with
  the per-dog breakdown for months with stays.
- **`RepositoryBase` has unimplemented overrides** that throw
  `NotImplementedException` (`RepositoryDogs/Tutors/PetSitter`). Check before
  calling; implement the stub you need. `RepositoryServices` does not derive from
  it — it spans four tables.
- **Walk/pet-sitting bookings have no stored duration**; the Google Calendar
  export assumes one hour.
- The dog screen lists **upcoming unpaid** services only; the tutor screen lists
  **every** unpaid service (it is the tutor's bill).
- **Schema vs README naming**: the schema/code use `Tutors` / `PetSitterTutors`,
  not README's Client / PetSitterClient. The schema wins — say so rather than
  silently picking one.

## Domain rules index (auto-attach by file, or read on demand)

Deep, task-specific guidance lives in these sibling rules (and, verbatim, in
`.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`). Read the relevant one **before** working in
that area:

| When you are… | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Adding/moving a screen, back-stack, row commands | `navigation-presentation` |
| Changing a table, column, DTO, repository query, delete cascade | `data-layer-schema` |
| Touching billing, payments, credit, paid/done flags, master password | `money-payments-credit` |
| Touching backup/restore, dog photos, export/save dialogs | `backup-restore-export` |
| Building/adjusting any `.axaml`, size, font, dialog | `styling-design-canvas` |
| Writing any `.axaml`, custom control, selector, binding | `avalonia-docs-connector` |
